## HomeGraph

This project has a HomeGraph MCP server (search, node, explore, spec tools, …). It is a tree-sitter symbol graph — use it for **in-repo structure**.

### When to call (path-first)

User task already names **one** in-repo relative path to a source file (e.g. `features/.../Foo.ets`) and is a code change → **Read that file and edit**; **do not call `homegraph_*`** (Skip is correct).

For how/mechanism/wiring, named Type/Component/`Type.member`, inheritance/subtypes, or in-repo `@kit`/`@ohos` **usages** when **no** single-file path: call `homegraph_explore` — **no Grep-first** storm. Domain keywords are enough when names are unknown.

Prefer the smallest tool when a name is already known: `callers`/`callees`/`node` for one symbol; `explore` for multi-file flows and usage inventories.

### Do not call HomeGraph

Skip every `homegraph_*` tool for topic file-lists, concept/UI-behavior with no named anchors, SDK/`@kit` **feature catalogs** (not usages), and literal pattern hunts. If a tool returns **Skip HomeGraph**, do not retry.

`@kit` usages in this repo ≠ SDK catalog. Usages → explore. Catalogs → SDK docs.

### After explore

Treat returned line-numbered source as already Read — do not re-grep/node/read the same symbols.

### Index lag

If a response starts with "⚠️ Some files referenced below were edited since the last index sync…", Read only those listed files.

### If `.homegraph/` doesn't exist

Ask the user whether to run `homegraph init -i`.
